<div class="ltx_page_main">
<div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">linear functional</h1>

<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<br class="ltx_break">
</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p">Let <math id="p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline"><mi>V</mi></math> be a <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">vector space</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/VectorSpace.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/vectorspace"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup> over a field <math id="p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline"><mi>K</mi></math>.
A <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">linear functional</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/LinearFunctional.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/dualmodule"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/functional"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/linearfunctional"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup></em> (or <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/homogeneouspolynomial1">linear form</a></em>) on <math id="p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline"><mi>V</mi></math>
is a <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/lineartransformation">linear mapping</a> <math id="p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\colon V\to K" display="inline"><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></math>,
where <math id="p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline"><mi>K</mi></math> is thought of as a one-dimensional vector space over itself.</p>
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p">The <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">collection</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Collection.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/collection"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup> of all linear functionals on <math id="p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline"><mi>V</mi></math>
can be made into a vector space
by defining <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">addition</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/addition"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/cardinalarithmetic"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup> and <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/ScalarMultiplication.html">scalar multiplication</a> <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/pointwise">pointwise</a>;
this vector space is called the <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">dual space</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/DualSpace.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/dualspace"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/banachspace"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/dualofstonerepresentationtheorem"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup> of <math id="p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline"><mi>V</mi></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="p4" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p">The term <span class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">linear functional</span> derives from
the case where <math id="p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline"><mi>V</mi></math> is a <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/functionspace">space of functions</a>
(see the entry on <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">functionals</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Functional.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/interpretationofintuitionisticlogicbymeansoffunctionals"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/intuitionisticlogic"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup> (<span class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">http://planetmath.org/Functional</span>)).
Some authors restrict the term to this case.
</p>
